### The media library as another pod service sees it (ExternalMediaApi)
### Service-to-service only. In the running stack catalog calls these with its s2s client-credentials token;
### the session cookie below is for driving them by hand.

### Resolve assets by id. Ids belonging to another store are simply absent from the response, which is what
### lets catalog use this as its ownership check before saving a product image.
GET {{SELLER_UI_URL}}/spg/content/api/v1/private/content/external/media?ids=1,2,3&store={{STORE_ID}}&pod={{POD_ID}}&lang={{LANG}}
Cookie: SESSION={{SESSION_ID}}

### Replace the whole reference set for one owner. Idempotent: send it twice, get the same rows.
PUT {{SELLER_UI_URL}}/spg/content/api/v1/private/content/external/media/usage?store={{STORE_ID}}&pod={{POD_ID}}&lang={{LANG}}
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: SESSION={{SESSION_ID}}

{
  "ownerKind": "PRODUCT",
  "ownerRef": "42",
  "ownerTitle": "Blue sneakers",
  "refs": [{"field": "image[0]", "assetId": 1}, {"field": "image[1]", "assetId": 2}]
}

### Release: the same call with no refs. There is no separate delete on purpose.
PUT {{SELLER_UI_URL}}/spg/content/api/v1/private/content/external/media/usage?store={{STORE_ID}}&pod={{POD_ID}}&lang={{LANG}}
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: SESSION={{SESSION_ID}}

{"ownerKind": "PRODUCT", "ownerRef": "42", "ownerTitle": "Blue sneakers", "refs": []}

### The asset now names the product that uses it, without content ever calling catalog
GET {{SELLER_UI_URL}}/spg/content/api/v1/private/content/media/1/usage?store={{STORE_ID}}&pod={{POD_ID}}&lang={{LANG}}
Cookie: SESSION={{SESSION_ID}}

### And deleting it is refused while the product holds it
DELETE {{SELLER_UI_URL}}/spg/content/api/v1/private/content/media/1?store={{STORE_ID}}&pod={{POD_ID}}&lang={{LANG}}
Cookie: SESSION={{SESSION_ID}}

### A store admin must NOT be able to write the usage index — that token is for services in the same pod
PUT {{SELLER_UI_URL}}/spg/content/api/v1/private/content/external/media/usage?store={{STORE_ID}}&pod={{POD_ID}}&lang={{LANG}}
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: SESSION={{STORE_ADMIN_SESSION_ID}}

{"ownerKind": "PRODUCT", "ownerRef": "42", "ownerTitle": "Blue sneakers", "refs": []}
